cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "How Machine-Checkable Is IAB Privacy Signaling? Syntax versus Meaning on the Wire"
message: If you use this codebook, statement dataset, or wild aggregates, please cite the preprint.
type: article
authors:
  - family-names: Sekowski
    given-names: Aleksander
date-released: "2026-08-26"
version: "1.0"
url: "https://github.com/aleksUIX/iab-privacy-checkability"
repository-code: "https://github.com/aleksUIX/iab-privacy-checkability"
abstract: >-
  IAB privacy signaling is a transport: the checkable layer is string
  shape, not a person-fact. 221 normative sentences from GPP, TCF,
  US Privacy, and OpenRTB privacy fields; 162 conformance statements;
  syntax versus meaning coding; a US web baseline from paper 3; CTV
  as the stress test for meaning.
keywords:
  - Global Privacy Platform
  - Transparency and Consent Framework
  - OpenRTB
  - connected TV
  - privacy signaling
  - protocol verification
